WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:04.535
A droplet entering a microchannel looks like progress

00:00:04.535 --> 00:00:08.109
toward a small diagnostic laboratory. The hard

00:00:08.109 --> 00:00:09.641
questions begin downstream.

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:18.817
Imagine taking a complex testing workflow and moving

00:00:18.817 --> 00:00:23.025
parts of it into channels so small that fluid behaviour

00:00:23.025 --> 00:00:24.709
becomes a design constraint.

00:00:32.450 --> 00:00:35.675
Specimen collection, sample transport and preparation

00:00:35.675 --> 00:00:39.974
can determine whether a miniature diagnostic device is

00:00:39.974 --> 00:00:40.511
useful.

00:00:47.450 --> 00:00:51.233
Microfluidic systems can organise small volumes and

00:00:51.233 --> 00:00:55.017
reactions, but sensitivity and specificity still depend

00:00:55.017 --> 00:00:57.179
on the biological assay.

00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:06.077
Finding an analytical signal requires distinguishing

00:01:06.077 --> 00:01:10.308
target detection, contamination, false results and the

00:01:10.308 --> 00:01:11.517
clinical situation.

00:01:17.450 --> 00:01:20.632
Sample processing, target capture and analytical

00:01:20.632 --> 00:01:24.874
specificity do not disappear when a device becomes

00:01:24.874 --> 00:01:27.525
smaller. Miniaturisation can add constraints.

00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:35.660
Manufacturability, reliable reagents, operator burden

00:01:35.660 --> 00:01:40.155
and clinical validation decide whether a clever

00:01:40.155 --> 00:01:42.081
microsystem becomes useful.

00:01:46.450 --> 00:01:50.582
The purpose of a chip is reliable detection in a real

00:01:50.582 --> 00:01:53.587
sample, not merely an attractive miniature flow path.
